# Every variable that Hydrograf reads (DEV-13.1, DEV-18.3). Copy this file to `.env`
# (git-ignored) and fill it in. A line that starts with `#` shows the default of an
# optional variable; secrets are set only here or in the environment, never committed.

# --- Database ---
# Required: the password of the PostGIS user (Docker Compose refuses to start without it).
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
# POSTGRES_DB=hydro_db
# POSTGRES_USER=hydro_user
# `db` inside Docker Compose, `localhost` when the API runs on the host.
# POSTGRES_HOST=localhost
# POSTGRES_PORT=5432
# Complete connection URL; when set it wins over the POSTGRES_* variables and over
# DATABASE_URL_OVERRIDE (Docker Compose sets it for the API container).
# DATABASE_URL=
# DATABASE_URL_OVERRIDE=
# Statement timeout of every database session [ms].
# DB_STATEMENT_TIMEOUT_MS=120000

# --- API ---
# DEBUG, INFO, WARNING or ERROR.
# LOG_LEVEL=INFO
# Comma-separated list of allowed CORS origins.
# CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost,http://localhost:8080,http://127.0.0.1,http://127.0.0.1:8080
# Directory of the pipeline outputs; the API finds the DEM raster there
# (VRT, then GeoTIFF).
# DEM_DIR=/data/nmt
# Explicit DEM raster for terrain profiles; wins over DEM_DIR.
# DEM_PATH=
# Stream distance raster for flow path points; default: file in DEM_DIR.
# STREAM_DISTANCE_PATH=
# Directory of frontend/data as the API sees it (nginx serves it under /data/); the
# terrain profile reads the analysis results manifest results/index.json and the
# water level rasters from its results/ subdirectory.
# FRONTEND_DATA_DIR=/frontend/data

# --- Admin panel ---
# Set ONE of these (ADMIN_API_KEY takes precedence; the file is read on every request).
# With neither, every route of /api/admin/ refuses (401, admin_key_not_configured).
# ADMIN_API_KEY=
# Path of a file that holds the key (Docker secret in production).
# ADMIN_API_KEY_FILE=

# --- Kartograf store ---
# The Kartograf store that Archiwista alone writes (ADR-066, ADR-067). Hydrograf reads it
# only through a closed set of an Archiwista project (`bootstrap --project PATH --set NAME`);
# while it is set, every download (`--bbox`, `--sheets`, `--boundary-file`, download_dem,
# download_landcover, prepare_area, analyze_watershed --download, the CN fallback) is
# refused. Empty: the private store <cache_dir>/kartograf (ADR-061), which the downloads
# write. The metadata cache stays in <cache_dir> either way.
# HYDROGRAF_KARTOGRAF_ROOT=

# --- Ecosystem GUIs ---
# The GUIs of the Nogat ecosystem that this deployment runs, for the menu „Aplikacje” of
# the top bar (ADR-082): the table `gui` of `[nogat]` in nogat.toml (Nogat DEV-15.4,
# DEV-18.1) as one JSON object, a registry name in lower case to an address (an http or
# https URL, or a path from / on this host); single quotes keep it one value. The API
# refuses to start with a value that is not such an object. Empty: the table `gui` of the
# nogat.toml of NOGAT_CONFIG, and without it no menu.
# HYDROGRAF_GUI='{"hydrolog": "http://127.0.0.1:8070/", "archiwista": "http://127.0.0.1:8090/"}'

# --- Public service (ADR-084) ---
# The deployment's nogat.toml (Nogat DEV-18.1). Its table `operator` of `[nogat]` (the
# operator, terms_effective, the processor and the mail provider) makes Hydrograf a
# public service: the regulamin at /regulamin.html, the statement and the link
# „Regulamin” under the map, the operator's e-mail under „Zgłoś uwagę” (DEV-15.7,
# DEV-15.8, DEV-15.12); the address of the regulamin's service is the entry `hydrograf`
# of the table `gui`. Docker Compose mounts this host file read-only into the API at
# /config/nogat.toml. Empty: no file, no regulamin, no footer. A change needs a restart
# of the API.
# NOGAT_CONFIG=/home/USER/.config/nogat/nogat.toml
# Requests per client address in a window [s] (DEV-15.9): pages and API routes; map
# tiles have ten times the limit, „Zgłoś uwagę” besides at most 5 reports in 5 minutes.
# HYDROGRAF_REQUEST_LIMIT=300
# HYDROGRAF_REQUEST_WINDOW=60
# The data_dir of the daily statistics <data_dir>/hydrograf/stats.jsonl (DEV-15.11), as
# the API sees it; in Docker /data, which is HYDROGRAF_DATA_PATH on the host, so set it
# only for an API run on the host.
# HYDROGRAF_DATA_DIR=/data

# --- Logs (Nogat DEV-12.4 to DEV-12.9) ---
# The state_dir of the API's logs, <state_dir>/hydrograf/logs/<kind>-YYYY-MM-DD.jsonl
# (access, app, lifecycle), which the API deletes after 14 days (DEV-12.6, DEV-18.1): the
# first of HYDROGRAF_STATE_DIR, NOGAT_STATE_DIR, `state_dir` of `[hydrograf]` or
# `[nogat]` in the nogat.toml of NOGAT_CONFIG; default ~/.local/state/nogat. Docker
# Compose reads NOGAT_STATE_DIR on the host: it mounts <NOGAT_STATE_DIR>/hydrograf
# (default ./state/hydrograf) at /state/hydrograf and sets NOGAT_STATE_DIR=/state inside;
# create that host directory once, writable by the API's UID 999, like data/:
# `install -d -m 0777 ~/.local/state/nogat/hydrograf`.
# HYDROGRAF_STATE_DIR=
# NOGAT_STATE_DIR=/home/USER/.local/state/nogat

# --- Docker Compose ---
# External port of the web interface.
# HYDROGRAF_PORT=8080
# A second instance on the same Docker host (`docker compose -p NAME --env-file NAME.env`)
# sets its own container prefix (containers <prefix>_db, <prefix>_api, <prefix>_nginx), its
# own port and its own host directories; the database volume and the network already carry
# the compose project's name. Relative paths are relative to the compose file.
# HYDROGRAF_CONTAINER_PREFIX=hydro
# HYDROGRAF_CACHE_PATH=./cache
# HYDROGRAF_DATA_PATH=./data
# HYDROGRAF_FRONTEND_DATA_PATH=./frontend/data
# HYDROGRAF_FRONTEND_TILES_PATH=./frontend/tiles
# Public host name of the application (the Cloudflare tunnel); informational, no code reads it.
# HYDROGRAF_PUBLIC_HOST=hydrograf-test.debever.pl
# TLS (production only): host name and the directory of the Docker secrets files.
# SERVER_NAME=
# SECRETS_DIR=./secrets
